WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.982
This query first creates daily revenue by department.

00:00:02.982 --> 00:00:06.322
Then a window SUM accumulates those daily values.

00:00:06.322 --> 00:00:10.947
The frame is explicit: from unbounded preceding through the current row.

00:00:10.947 --> 00:00:15.297
Run it and watch the cumulative revenue increase within each department.

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:19.132
The partition restarts the running total for each department.

00:00:19.132 --> 00:00:23.872
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:23.872 --> 00:00:29.587
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:31.687
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:37.097
In a real setting such as a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region,

00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:43.142
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.612
before discussing syntax.

00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:50.400
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
